(1789430400000) would leave 2850 as a lower-high failure after 2771 and shift primary_regime toward trading-range or transition-unclear.", "Continued bar-by-bar overlap inside 2633.31-2786.81 without a new high keeps the current phase as a range at the highs rather than a resumed spike."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790524799999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The pullback from 2850.00 held above the bar-83 breakout zone and above the 2358.62-2850.00 midpoint; no close below 2633.31 occurred, so the higher-low structure of the bull leg is still intact.", "Lows since bar 101 are rising (2633.31 -> 2640.00 -> 2665.14 -> 2682.11) and closes recovered from 2647.90 (bar 101) to 2694.96-2717.24 (bars 116-118), a sideways-to-up drift typical of a bull flag rather than active distribution.", "The stall is not a strong bear reversal: bars 87-120 contain no large bear trend bar that broke out of the range on the downside with follow-through.", "Volume eased from 8.4-9.0M on the bar 83-86 trend bars to mostly 1.9-4.1M on bars 109-120, which is consistent with a quiet pullback inside a bull trend.", "The bar-83 spike and the bars 66-86 leg (about 2500 to 2804.59) mean a bull breakout above 2721.75 and 2740.42 could quickly re-establish trend structure."], "evidence_for": ["No new high for 34 bars: swing highs step down 2804.59 (bar 86) -> 2786.81 (bar 94) -> 2740.42 (bar 107) -> 2721.75 (bar 108).", "Bars 87-120 overlap between 2633.31 and 2786.81 with many small bars and mixed closes, so two-sided overlap is now the largest block of the window.", "The bar-83 spike to 2850.00 was not accepted: price trades back near 2688.80, around the 2690-2700 pre-spike resistance zone and below bar 83's close of 2723.15.", "The 13 most recent bars (108-120) are a tight range 2665.14-2721.75 (about 2% tall) with closes near mid-range, a breakout-mode range rather than a directional leg.", "Bar 96 was a large bear bar (open 2726.71, close 2659.00) and bar 101 closed 2647.90 below the bar-96 low 2648.49, so the pullback already produced a marginal lower low."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window: 120 closed H4 bars, open_time 1788796800000 through close_time 1790524799999; first bar opens 2468.71, last bar closes 2688.80 (+8.9%), path = early range, bear leg, bull leg, range.", "Early two-sided range, bars 1-23: contained between 2411.04 (bar 18 low) and 2520.68 (bar 11 high); closes repeatedly returned to 2460-2500.", "Bar 24 (open 2457.12) spiked to 2680.00 and closed 2555.52, a large bull spike out of the early range; bars 24-34 then overlapped in a 2503-2609 band and no close exceeded 2555.52 again until bar 65.", "Bear leg bars 44-49: high 2609.02 (bar 44, reversal bar closing 2514.07) to low 2358.62 (bar 49) = -9.6%; bars 48 (close 2423.29) and 49 (close 2412.95) closed near their lows.", "Bull leg bars 49-86: 2358.62 low to 2850.00 (bar 83 high) and 2804.59 (bar 86 high) = +20.8%; trend bars at bar 66 (close 2578.60), bar 67 (close 2636.28), bar 83 (open 2658.81, high 2850.00, close 2723.15) and bar 84 (close 2754.31).", "Bars 87-120 stall: no close above bar 86 close 2775.61; swing highs step down 2804.59 (bar 86) -> 2786.81 (bar 94) -> 2740.42 (bar 107) -> 2721.75 (bar 108), with the pullback low at 2633.31 (bar 101).", "Bars 108-120 form a tight range 2665.14 (bar 116 low) to 2721.75 (bar 108 high); bar ranges in that block are mostly under 25 points and closes stay between 2677.28 and 2717.24.", "Final bar (open 2709.21, high 2715.35, low 2682.11, close 2688.80) is a bear bar closing in the lower part of its own range and of the 13-bar range; no follow-through in either direction.", "Optional corroboration: per-bar volume fell from 8.4-9.0M on bars 83-86 to mostly 1.9-4.1M on bars 109-120."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "trading-range", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Early two-sided range before the bar-24 spike; repeated tests of 2500-2520 on the top and 2440-2460 on the bottom.", "end_time_ms": 1789127999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2411.04", "start_time_ms": 1788796800000, "upper_boundary": "2520.68"}, {"description": "Bear swing from the bar-44 reversal high down to the bar-49 low; two large bear bars closed near their lows at the end of the leg.", "end_time_ms": 1789502399999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789416000000, "upper_boundary": "2609.02"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the bar-49 low to the bar-86 high, with higher highs and higher lows and a final spike wick to 2850.00 on bar 83 (open 2658.81, close 2723.15); highest close in the leg is 2775.61 (bar 86).", "end_time_ms": 1790035199999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Trading range at the highs after the bull leg: bars 87-120 overlap between the bar-101 pullback low and the bar-94 high, with a descending series of swing highs (2804.59, 2786.81, 2740.42, 2721.75) and no new high for 34 bars.", "end_time_ms": 1790524799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2786.81"}, {"description": "Tight trading range / breakout mode, bars 108-120: about 2% tall, small overlapping bars with closes near mid-range, boundaries respected on both sides and the last bar bearish but still inside the range.", "end_time_ms": 1790524799999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2665.14", "start_time_ms": 1790337600000, "upper_boundary": "2721.75"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull resumption: a bull trend bar closing above 2740.42 and then above 2786.81 with follow-through would shift the read toward a bull-trend breakout-spike phase.", "Bear shift: a strong bear bar closing below 2665.14, then acceptance below 2633.31, would flip the Always-In to short and raise an MTR-like top read from the 2804.59 lower high.", "Continued range: continued overlapping bars between 2665.14 and 2740.42 keep the breakout-mode range classification, with both tails of the range still available.", "Breakout resolution: the first bar closing outside 2665.14-2721.75 with follow-through in the next one or two bars would resolve the range's direction; an immediate reversal back inside would instead confirm failed-breakout behavior."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2749.43", "close_time_ms": 1790107199999, "high": "2761.63", "low": "2745.55", "open": "2751.61", "open_time_ms": 1790103600000, "volume": "2205819.744"}, {"close": "2748.87", "close_time_ms": 1790110799999, "high": "2756.31", "low": "2746.89", "open": "2749.43", "open_time_ms": 1790107200000, "volume": "1331804.586"}, {"close": "2746.61", "close_time_ms": 1790114399999, "high": "2752.18", "low": "2746.61", "open": "2748.87", "open_time_ms": 1790110800000, "volume": "914145.546"}, {"close": "2751.88", "close_time_ms": 1790117999999, "high": "2757.12", "low": "2737.75", "open": "2746.61", "open_time_ms": 1790114400000, "volume": "2005458.779"}, {"close": "2752.43", "close_time_ms": 1790121599999, "high": "2767.3", "low": "2749.04", "open": "2751.79", "open_time_ms": 1790118000000, "volume": "1687743.157"}, {"close": "2759.21", "close_time_ms": 1790125199999, "high": "2764.34", "low": "2749.28", "open": "2752.43", "open_time_ms": 1790121600000, "volume": "1686669.005"}, {"close": "2750.89", "close_time_ms": 1790128799999, "high": "2770.67", "low": "2746.19", "open": "2759.2", "open_time_ms": 1790125200000, "volume": "2039711.527"}, {"close": "2761.1", "close_time_ms": 1790132399999, "high": "2761.1", "low": "2745.2", "open": "2750.89", "open_time_ms": 1790128800000, "volume": "1429026.926"}, {"close": "2772.99", "close_time_ms": 1790135999999, "